      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T21:09:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of adding a new API, how about just adding more flags for FPDF_SaveAsCopy()?\n\nMany APIs treat the flags as a set of bits, but FPDF_REMOVE_SECURITY is broken in that it\u0027s 11b, which is the same as FPDF_INCREMENTAL | FPDF_NO_INCREMENTAL. One way to fix this is to have FPDF_REMOVE_SECURITY_DEPRECATED \u003d 3 and add FPDF_REMOVE_SECURITY \u003d 4. Then this CL can use 8 as the next bit.\n\nThere\u0027s also crbug.com/42270430, which I optomistically assigned to myself in April 2020. I guess I got distracted.",
